cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this research compendium, please cite it as below."
title: "Guidance and surveillance capability for bystander Staphylococcus aureus tetracycline resistance under doxy-PEP: a three-stream evidence audit — research compendium"
abstract: >-
  Complete computational research compendium (code, coded data, and manuscript) supporting
  the measurement-inheritance analysis of doxy-PEP and bystander tetracycline-resistant
  Staphylococcus aureus. Contains no participant-level trial data. Licensing is
  content-specific: the SOFTWARE (src/, tests/, scripts/, Makefile) is MIT (LICENSE-CODE);
  the manuscript TEXT and figures are CC BY 4.0 (LICENSE-TEXT); externally-sourced third-party
  inputs are neither relicensed nor redistributed (see THIRD_PARTY_DATA.md). The `license`
  field below is the SOFTWARE license.
type: software
